    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Problem\n\nneed a way to restore arguments without affecting the buffer list (adding buffers)\n\nsee #42002 and #42009 \n\n### Expected behavior\n\nArguments can be restored without adding buffers.\n\nIdeas:\n1. A new 'sessionoptions' flag that restores args\n2. some custom logic of smart removing argument buffers (without affecting order of the final buffer list)\n",
    "closed_at": null,
    "closed_by": null,
    "comment_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> need a way to restore arguments without affecting the buffer list (adding buffers)\n\nI don't think this really makes sense. When I mentioned \"some sort of 'sessionoptions' feature\" in https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42009 I was *assuming* there is a feature gap in session, but I didn't think beyond that. Maybe there is a gap, but \"add args without adding buffers\" isn't it.\n\nFor `:restart`, the first step is https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42009#issuecomment-5772018158 .",
